{"event_id":"EVT-000080","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-29T20:15:00.407Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260829T200425712334Z","run_id":"RUN-I2-011-20260829T201156728324Z","requirement_id":"I2-011","event_type":"validator_feedback_possible_reversal","iteration":4,"prior_feedback_history":["Repair the DIRECT_CALCULATION formula so every declared operandTerm is semantically used: the current SPARQL only compares the two method-force values and merely records shapeCoefficient=0.6 and loadPatchAspectRatio=1.3 without incorporating them into the I2.3.2.1(iii) calculation or explicitly tying that calculated lower-bound force to the result. Preserve the applicable PC6/PC7-and-bulbous-bow boundary, use method (iv) as the prescribed determination with the method (iii) force as the not-less-than lower bound (using tolerance for derived decimal comparisons), and retain the declared units and controlled constants.","The formula operands are now used, but repair the derived comparison semantics: do not require bowDesignForce to equal method (iv) via a tolerance, since the regulatory condition is a not-less-than constraint. Require the reported bowDesignForce to be at least the prescribed method (iv) force and at least the calculated method (iii) lower bound, with tolerances scaled from the expected comparison values rather than from the reported value. Also reconcile the force units before comparing or deriving values: method (iii) and method (iv) are in MegaN while bowDesignForce is in KiloN, so apply the explicit 1000 conversion (or use a consistent unit). Preserve the PC6/PC7 plus bulbous-bow applicability boundary and the declared constants.","The candidate otherwise preserves the applicability boundary, owners, units, operands, comparison direction, and expected-value-scaled tolerance, but its DIRECT_CALCULATION query uses the unregistered ABS function. Replace each ABS(?expected) with an allowed min/max or explicit piecewise expression using only the permitted arithmetic and comparisons; retain tolerance scaling from the expected method (iv) and calculated method (iii) values."],"current_feedback":"Remove the non-applicable partition constraints that are not stated by the requirement. The current sh:or incorrectly requires every PC1\u2013PC5 ship to have bulbousBowPresent=true, so a PC1\u2013PC5 ship without a bulbous bow fails even though the rule is inapplicable; the BulbousBowAbsentShape also imposes an unnecessary polarClass class check. Encode the applicability boundary so only ships with polarClass PC6 or PC7 and bulbousBowPresent=true receive the force, operand, unit, and formula checks, while all other ships are permitted without invented constraints. Preserve the existing DIRECT_CALCULATION formula, 1000 MegaN-to-KiloN conversion, expected-value-scaled piecewise tolerances, and not-less-than comparisons.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
